## Forge Ship Workflow

Run `forge ship "<feature description>"` to start the AI-assisted 6-checkpoint pipeline:

| Checkpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **spec** | Generate/validate feature spec in `.forge/specs/<slug>/spec.md` |
| **arch** | Multi-role architecture debate → ADR document |
| **test** | Generate failing TDD test stubs (write tests first) |
| **breakdown** | Decompose spec into atomic task list |
| **code** | Generate/iterate code until tests pass |
| **ship** | Hygiene + scan + lint readiness check |

```bash
forge ship "add user authentication"   # full pipeline
forge ship --from test                 # resume from a checkpoint
forge ship --quick                     # spec + code only (skip arch/breakdown)
forge ship --dry-run                   # preview without executing
```

## Forge Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `forge lint` | Validate `.forge/conventions.json` — run before commit |
| `forge scan security` | OWASP Top-10 scan — run before every PR |
| `forge clean --check` | Hygiene check — must be green before commit |
| `forge doctor` | Validate `forge.config.yml` and environment |
| `forge context generate` | Refresh `.forge/knowledge-index.json` |
| `forge explain <file>` | Ask the LLM to explain code |

## Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `forge.config.yml` | Project configuration (ship checkpoints, LLM, security) |
| `.forge/conventions.json` | Machine-readable convention registry (`forge lint`) |
| `.forge/hygiene.yml` | Managed/scratch file policy (`forge clean`) |
| `.forge/manifest` | Managed-file registry |
| `.forge/knowledge-index.json` | **Forge knowledge base index** — patterns, principles, compliance rules injected into every LLM call by `forge ship` |
| `.forge/instructions/global.instructions.md` | LLM instructions for Copilot/Cursor/Claude |
| `.forge/specs/` | Ship-workflow artefacts (auto-generated) |

## Injected Knowledge

The file `.forge/knowledge-index.json` contains the forge knowledge base:
patterns, principles, compliance frameworks, NFR models, and reference
architectures. `forge ship` automatically selects relevant entries (top-5 by
tag score) and injects them into every LLM call as a `<knowledge>` block.

AI tools can read `.forge/knowledge-index.json` directly to surface these
patterns without running forge.

## AI Conventions

1. **Run `forge lint`** before committing — validates `.forge/conventions.json`
2. **Write failing tests first** — `forge ship` checkpoint 3 (test) enforces this
3. **Run `forge scan security` before every PR** — fix all findings
4. **Keep `forge clean --check` green** — no unmanifested scratch files
5. **Never hardcode secrets** — environment variables only
